    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Adjectives ending in -el, -en, -er",
     "texto": [
      "They lose the **e** when you add another one:\n\n- simpel → simpel**t** → **simple**\n- åben → åben**t** → **åbne**\n- sikker → sikker**t** → **sikre**\n- gammel → gammel**t** → **gamle**\n- sulten → **sultne**\n\nAnd the same goes for nouns: et kapitel → **kapitlet**, en regel → **reglen**."
     ],
     "tutora": "pensando"
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "kende or vide",
     "texto": [
      "- **kende** = to know (people, places): **Kender** du den restaurant?\n- **vide** = to know (a fact): Det **ved** jeg ikke.\n\nIn English both are «know», but in Danish they're different: kende ≠ vide. Easy!\n\nPresent: kender / **ved** · Past: kendte / **vidste**"
     ],
     "tutora": "contenta"
    },
